  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for curl",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for curl fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-5545: wrong reuse of HTTP Negotiate connection (bsc#1262632).\n- CVE-2026-5773: wrong reuse of SMB connection (bsc#1262633).\n- CVE-2026-6253: proxy credentials leak over redirect-to proxy (bsc#1262635).\n- CVE-2026-6276: stale custom cookie host causes cookie leak (bsc#1262636).\n- CVE-2026-6429: netrc credential leak with reused proxy connection (bsc#1262638).\n- CVE-2026-7168: cross-proxy Digest auth state leak (bsc#1263440).\n- CVE-2026-8926: password leak with netrc and user in URL (bsc#1268412).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
